    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2093233892102991910",
      "url": "https://x.com/koolkrypto223/status/2093233892102991910",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/koolkrypto223/status/2093233892102991910",
      "text": "Caught the meat of the $2000>$2400 $ETH move, only major I'm trimming now. I think it'll continue to perform reasonably well in dollar terms (denominator trending to zero innit) but it's back to the usual unhappy middleground for $ETH vs other crypto majors\n\nbitcoin:native and ethereum:0x68749665ff8d2d112fa859aa293f07a622782f38 are a better expression of debasement\n$SOL has more upcoming catalysts (SIMDs meaningfully changing issuance, higher beta overall and more consumer facing apps)\n$HYPE is $HYPE \ud83d\udc51\n\nI think if your view is that Clarity/SEC/CFTC regs are coming that help $ETH DeFi onboard billions more in TVL, specific DeFi protocols that more directly monetize that TVL like $AAVE, $ENA, $MORPHO etc probably catch a stronger bid.\n\nIf you just think Tom Lee comes in swinging or finds success with a $STRC clone, probably better to just own $BMNR.\n\n$HOOD and $LIT are just better beta to RH chain\n\nMy initial trade thesis for $ETH going into this was that it was underowned, used too much as a short leg for the exact trades I listed above, and had a good setup for a pop. After that has played out, I'm not really seeing what would drive it's outperformance relative to the market. Keeping my $2400/2800 call spreads for October, but not really getting the impression I need to go extremely out of the money on $ETH like I feel for $HYPE and bitcoin:native.",
